---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Customer Churn Prediction — Pradeep Loganathan',
  description:
    'Deep dive into Pradeep Loganathan’s telecom customer churn prediction project using XGBoost, threshold optimization, SHAP and customer risk scoring.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>

  <!-- =====================================================
       HERO
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8 lg:py-32">

      <div class="max-w-4xl">

        <a
          href="/#projects"
          class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent"
        >
          ← Back to projects
        </a>

        <p class="mt-10 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
          Deep Dive · Machine Learning
        </p>

        <h1 class="mt-4 text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">
          Customer Churn Prediction
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-8 text-muted">
          Predicting customer churn and turning model probabilities
          into actionable retention priorities.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">

          <a
            href="https://github.com/iampradeeploganathan/churn-prediction"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="btn btn-primary"
          >
            View GitHub ↗
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://churn-prediction-pradeep.streamlit.app/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="btn btn-primary"
          >
            View Live Prediction App ↗
          </a>
          <a
            href="/#projects"
            class="btn"
          >
            ← All Projects
          </a>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       PROJECT SNAPSHOT
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="border-y border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-8">

      <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Dataset</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">7,043</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">customers</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Initial Features</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">33</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">columns</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Churn Rate</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">26.54%</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">of customers</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Final Recall</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">78.34%</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">threshold 0.30</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       01 EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
      01 · Executive Summary
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      From prediction to prioritization
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-8 max-w-4xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-muted">

      <p>
        I built a telecom customer churn prediction system using
        the IBM Telco Customer Churn dataset.
      </p>

      <p>
        The workflow covered data cleaning, exploratory data analysis,
        encoding, train/test splitting, model comparison, XGBoost,
        threshold optimization, SHAP interpretation and customer
        risk scoring.
      </p>

      <p>
        The important part was not simply predicting whether a customer
        would churn. The model produces a churn probability which is
        converted into a risk level and a recommended retention action.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       02 SYSTEM WORKFLOW
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="border-y border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
        02 · System Workflow
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        How the system works
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-5">

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-6 dark:border-gray-700">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">01</span>
          <h3 class="mt-4 font-bold">Customer Data</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-6 dark:border-gray-700">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">02</span>
          <h3 class="mt-4 font-bold">Data Cleaning</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-6 dark:border-gray-700">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">03</span>
          <h3 class="mt-4 font-bold">Model Training</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-6 dark:border-gray-700">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">04</span>
          <h3 class="mt-4 font-bold">Threshold Optimization</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-6 dark:border-gray-700">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">05</span>
          <h3 class="mt-4 font-bold">Risk Classification</h3>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       03 DATASET
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
      03 · Dataset
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      Understanding the data
    </h2>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">
      The project uses the IBM Telco Customer Churn dataset with
      7,043 customers and 33 initial columns.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">

      <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">Target</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">Churn Value</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">Stayed</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">5,174</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">customers</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">Churned</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">1,869</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">customers</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">Churn Rate</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">26.54%</p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       04 DATA PREPARATION
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="border-y border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
        04 · Data Preparation
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        Cleaning before modelling
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Numeric Conversion</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
            Total Charges was initially treated as an object/string
            and converted to numeric.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Categorical Encoding</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
            Binary variables were encoded as 0/1 and multi-category
            variables were one-hot encoded.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Scaling</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
            Numerical features were standardized for Logistic Regression.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Tree Models</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
            Tree-based models did not require feature scaling.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       05 LEAKAGE CONTROL
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
      05 · Leakage Control
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      Features deliberately removed
    </h2>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">
      Some variables were excluded because they were identifiers,
      redundant, geographic-specific, post-outcome information,
      or potentially contained information unavailable at prediction time.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">

      {
        [
          'CustomerID',
          'Count',
          'Country',
          'State',
          'City',
          'Zip Code',
          'Lat Long',
          'Latitude',
          'Longitude',
          'Churn Label',
          'Churn Score',
          'CLTV',
          'Churn Reason',
        ].map((feature) => (
          <span class="rounded-full border px-4 py-2 text-sm dark:border-gray-700">
            {feature}
          </span>
        ))
      }

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       06 EDA
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="border-y border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
        06 · Exploratory Data Analysis
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        What the data showed
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-accent">Contract</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">
            Month-to-month customers churned more
          </h3>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-muted">
            <p>Month-to-month <strong class="text-current">42.71%</strong></p>
            <p>One year <strong class="text-current">11.27%</strong></p>
            <p>Two year <strong class="text-current">2.83%</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-accent">Tenure</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">
            Churned customers had shorter tenure
          </h3>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-muted">
            <p>Stayed <strong class="text-current">37.57 months</strong></p>
            <p>Churned <strong class="text-current">17.98 months</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-accent">Monthly Charges</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">
            Churned customers paid more monthly
          </h3>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-muted">
            <p>Stayed <strong class="text-current">$61.27</strong></p>
            <p>Churned <strong class="text-current">$74.44</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-accent">Payment Method</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">
            Electronic check had higher observed churn
          </h3>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-muted">
            <p>Electronic check <strong class="text-current">45.29%</strong></p>
            <p>Mailed check <strong class="text-current">19.11%</strong></p>
            <p>Bank transfer <strong class="text-current">16.71%</strong></p>
            <p>Credit card <strong class="text-current">15.24%</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-accent">Internet Service</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">
            Fiber optic customers had higher observed churn
          </h3>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-muted">
            <p>Fiber optic <strong class="text-current">41.89%</strong></p>
            <p>DSL <strong class="text-current">18.96%</strong></p>
            <p>No internet <strong class="text-current">7.41%</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-accent">Technical Support</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">
            Support was associated with lower churn
          </h3>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-muted">
            <p>No tech support <strong class="text-current">41.6%</strong></p>
            <p>Tech support <strong class="text-current">15.2%</strong></p>
            <p>No internet <strong class="text-current">7.4%</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-muted">
        These findings describe observed associations in the dataset;
        they should not be interpreted as causal relationships.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       07 MODEL COMPARISON
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
      07 · Model Comparison
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      Three models, different trade-offs
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-12 overflow-x-auto">

      <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] border-collapse text-left">

        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b dark:border-gray-700">
            <th class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold">Model</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold">Accuracy</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold">Precision</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold">Recall</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold">F1</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold">ROC-AUC</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody>

          <tr class="border-b dark:border-gray-700">
            <td class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold">Logistic Regression</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">74.31%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">51.05%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">78.07%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">61.73%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">84.87%</td>
          </tr>

          <tr class="border-b dark:border-gray-700">
            <td class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold">Random Forest</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">79.35%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">63.70%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">51.60%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">57.02%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">83.33%</td>
          </tr>

          <tr class="border-b dark:border-gray-700">
            <td class="px-4 py-4 font-semibold">XGBoost</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">80.62%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">65.83%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">56.15%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">60.61%</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4">85.57%</td>
          </tr>

        </tbody>

      </table>

    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">
      XGBoost had the strongest overall initial performance, but Logistic
      Regression had higher recall at the default threshold. That distinction
      became important because the project prioritized identifying churners.
    </p>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       08 THRESHOLD OPTIMIZATION
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="border-y border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
        08 · Threshold Optimization
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        Accuracy wasn't enough
      </h2>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">
        A false negative means an actual churner was predicted as someone
        who would stay. For a retention use case, that means missing an
        opportunity to intervene.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">

        <div class="rounded-3xl border p-8 dark:border-gray-700">

          <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">
            Default threshold
          </p>

          <p class="mt-3 text-5xl font-bold">0.50</p>

          <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 gap-5">

            <div>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">Accuracy</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">80.62%</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">Precision</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">65.83%</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">Recall</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">56.15%</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">False Negatives</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">164</p>
            </div>

          </div>

          <p class="mt-5 text-muted">
            True Positives: <strong class="text-current">210</strong>
          </p>

        </div>


        <div class="rounded-3xl border-2 border-accent/30 p-8 dark:border-accent/30">

          <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">
            Selected threshold
          </p>

          <p class="mt-3 text-5xl font-bold">0.30</p>

          <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 gap-5">

            <div>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">Accuracy</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">77.43%</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">Precision</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">54.89%</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">Recall</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">78.34%</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">False Negatives</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">81</p>
            </div>

          </div>

          <p class="mt-5 text-muted">
            True Positives: <strong class="text-current">293</strong>
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>


      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Recall</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">+22.19 pp</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">56.15% → 78.34%</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">False Negatives</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">164 → 81</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">83 fewer missed churners</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border p-7 dark:border-gray-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Trade-off</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">FP ↑</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">109 → 241</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-muted">
        For this project, 0.30 was selected based on the recall/F1 trade-off
        and the retention objective. It is not presented as a universally
        optimal telecom threshold.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       09 CONFUSION MATRIX
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
      09 · Confusion Matrix
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      What changed at threshold 0.30?
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-12 overflow-x-auto">

      <table class="w-full max-w-3xl border-collapse text-center">

        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th></th>
            <th class="px-6 py-4">Actual Stay</th>
            <th class="px-6 py-4">Actual Churn</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody>

          <tr class="border">
            <th class="border px-6 py-6 text-left">
              Predicted Stay
            </th>

            <td class="border px-6 py-6">
              <span class="block text-sm text-muted">TN</span>
              <strong class="text-3xl">794</strong>
            </td>

            <td class="border px-6 py-6">
              <span class="block text-sm text-muted">FN</span>
              <strong class="text-3xl">81</strong>
            </td>
          </tr>

          <tr class="border">
            <th class="border px-6 py-6 text-left">
              Predicted Churn
            </th>

            <td class="border px-6 py-6">
              <span class="block text-sm text-muted">FP</span>
              <strong class="text-3xl">241</strong>
            </td>

            <td class="border px-6 py-6">
              <span class="block text-sm text-muted">TP</span>
              <strong class="text-3xl">293</strong>
            </td>
          </tr>

        </tbody>

      </table>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- =====================================================
       10 SHAP
  ====================================================== -->

  <section class="border-y border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-8">

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
        10 · Model Interpretation
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        What was the model relying on?
      </h2>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">
        SHAP was used to understand which features were influencing the
        model's predictions. The values explain model behavior; they do
        not establish causation.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">

        {
          [
            'Contract_Two year',
            'Tenure Months',
            'Dependents',
